/**
 * A `mock`-type channel-adapter gateway - deliberately NOT `http`.
 *
 * This is the regression net for a real bug: RouterGenerator used to mount the
 * bx-ai Gateway surface (`route( "/gateways" ).toAiGateway()`) only when a
 * gateway of type `http` existed. Every push-only project therefore got no
 * `/gateways/interactions/:requestID` routes - the human-in-the-loop approval
 * channel - so such an agent could PAUSE for an approval it had no endpoint to
 * answer. `http` is one gateway among many and must not gate the others.
 *
 * `mock` is used rather than a real push type (telegram/slack/...) on purpose:
 * it is a genuine channel-adapter entry for the generator's purposes, and it
 * opens no socket and needs no credential, so it is safe to boot in CI.
 */
class {

	function configure() {
		return { type : "mock" };
	}

}
